course: dictionary
lesson: 15441
title: Steadiness: firm, even and calm
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Steadiness is a noun, so it names a quality. It comes from the adjective steady. Steady means not shaking, even, or calm, and steadiness is the quality of being steady. When you meet it in a text, read the words around it to find out which sense the author means.
explain: «Maya kept her hand steady, and the wire never touched the hoop.» Here the clues are hand, wire and hoop. Steadiness means being firm and not shaking. Ask yourself: what word would fit here? Then try your meaning in the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
explain: Steadiness can also mean calm and reliable. «When the alarm rang, the nurse's steadiness calmed everyone.» An alarm makes people panic, so her steadiness must mean staying calm and sensible. In a graph, steadiness means a steady rate with no jumps.
fact: Steadiness is a noun, and it is uncountable: you say «more steadiness», not «a steadiness».
fact: «Steadiness» can mean being firm and not shaking or wobbling, as in «Her steadiness on the balance beam».
fact: «Steadiness» can mean being regular and even, with no sudden changes, as in «the steadiness of the line on the graph».
fact: «Steadiness» can mean being calm, sensible and reliable, especially in a crisis.
fact: Steady is the adjective and steadiness is the noun: «steady hands» show steadiness.
exercise: «Her steadiness on the balance beam helped her land every move.» What does steadiness mean here? | Being hungry | *Being firm and not wobbling | Being very old | Being loud and fast
exercise: «The line on the graph showed steadiness, with no sudden jumps.» What does steadiness mean in this sentence? | Being firm and not shaking | Being calm in a crisis | Being loud and busy | *Being regular and even, without sudden changes
exercise: «The nurse's steadiness calmed everyone during the emergency.» What does steadiness show about the nurse? | Fast and rushed | Silly and loud | *Calm, sensible and reliable
test: «With steadiness, Maya held the wire still while she moved the hoop.» What is steadiness in this sentence? | Being noisy | *Being firm and not shaking | Being late | Being sleepy
test: «Tom's steadiness in the crisis made the whole team feel safe.» What does steadiness show about Tom? | Silly and loud | Hungry and tired | Fast and rushed | *Calm, sensible and reliable
exam: «The runner kept a steady pace, and her steadiness helped her win.» What does steadiness mean here? | Being firm and not shaking | *Being regular and even, without sudden changes | Being very old | Being angry
